{"parentUuid":"a29ca6af-23e1-489e-bf37-c92b9ccced46","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfRFcjCL2Azo3KPNZoYDJ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"If you mean the two LowTalker entries in the Input menu, that's two separate apps. Studious's Input menu reads:\n\n```\nU.S.\nLowTalker        ← /Applications/LowTalker.app (release)\nLowTalker Dev    ← /Applications/LowTalker Dev.app (development build)\n```\n\nEach build carries and installs its own input method with its own identifier: `ai.promptctl.low-talker.inputmethod.dictation` and `ai.promptctl.low-talker.dev.inputmethod.dictation`. That way a development build can sit next to the release without either overwriting the other (`Sources/Flavors/Flavor.swift:120`). LowTalker Dev.app was installed on studious on Sep 24 for earlier testing, and it put its input method in `~/Library/Input Methods` then.\n\nIf you mean the two entries I listed per build: a macOS input method has one entry for the input method as a whole, and one for each mode it offers. LowTalker offers a single mode, `.dictation.text`. Only the whole-method entry decides whether it's actually on, which is why the step reads that one.\n\nStudious is supposed to be the clean Mac for the zero-dialogs test, so the Dev build shouldn't be on it. I'd remove LowTalker Dev.app and its input method from there. Say the word and I'll do it. One catch: macOS keeps a removed input method's registration around, left as an entry with an empty name (low-input-method-s71.ssn, 2026-09-22 comment)."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":473,"cache_read_input_tokens":133575,"output_tokens":770,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":275},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":473,"ephemeral_5m_input_tok